  "worked_solution": "Using the fact that the dot product is linear in the first variable, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3a+b)\\cdot c+(2b-2c)\\cdot d & =(3a)\\cdot c+b\\cdot c+(2b)\\cdot d-(2c)\\cdot d \\\\  & =3(a\\cdot c)+b\\cdot c+2(b\\cdot d)-2(c\\cdot d).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we can use the fact that the dot product is symmetric to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(a\\cdot c)+b\\cdot c+2(b\\cdot d)-2(c\\cdot d) & =3(c\\cdot a)+c\\cdot b+2(b\\cdot d)-2(d\\cdot c).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the values for $c\\cdot a,$ $c\\cdot b,$ $b\\cdot d,$ and $d\\cdot c,$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(c\\cdot a)+c\\cdot b+2(b\\cdot d)-2(d\\cdot c) & =3(3)+(-2)+2(-1)-2(2) \\\\  & =9-2-2-4 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(3a+b)\\cdot c+(2b-2c)\\cdot d=1.$",
